# Local secrets for `vite dev` / `wrangler dev` (the `env.dev` environment).
# Copy to `.dev.vars` (or `.dev.vars.dev`, which takes precedence for --env dev)
# and fill in. Plain vars (SITE_URL, ENVIRONMENT, EMAIL_FROM, EMAIL_REPLY_TO)
# live in `wrangler.jsonc` under `env.dev.vars`; only secrets belong here.
# Staging and production secrets are set with `wrangler secret put --env <env>`
# (the schema is `workerSecretsSchema` in `@smog/config/env/worker`).

# Required. At least 32 characters; `openssl rand -base64 32` makes one.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=dev-only-secret-change-me-0123456789abcdef

# Optional. Leave empty to hide the provider (dev works without them).
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
APPLE_CLIENT_ID=
APPLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
APPLE_APP_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER=be.zias.smog

# Optional in dev, required in staging/production (`wrangler secret put`).
# When set, sign-up, sign-in, password reset, email code and magic link
# requests need a Turnstile token (`x-captcha-response`), and rpc mutations
# behind `requireTurnstile` need one in `x-turnstile-token`.
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
# Its public pair, TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY, is a var in `wrangler.jsonc`
# (`env.<env>.vars`), not a secret. Production needs both before launch:
# without the site key the web shows no widget and the guarded auth calls
# fail. Staging uses Cloudflare's always-pass test keys.

# Optional. The OpenPanel client the analytics relay (`/api/analytics`)
# forwards with; without both, consented events are accepted and dropped
# with a warning. OPENPANEL_API_URL is a var (default
# https://analytics.zias.be/api), not a secret.
OPENPANEL_CLIENT_ID=
OPENPANEL_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Dev sign-in: the seeded admin `admin@smog.test` has the DEV-ONLY password
# `smog-dev-admin` (packages/db/seed/dev.sql). Emails (verification links,
# codes, magic links) are not sent in dev: read them at /dev/mail.

# Optional. Mux Video (admin video uploads and the asset picker). Without
# both token values the admin offers only a pasted playback id, and
# /api/webhooks/mux answers 503 without the webhook signing secret.
# Staging/production: `wrangler secret put MUX_TOKEN_ID --env <env>` (and
# the others); production needs them before launch (phase 8). They stay
# commented out here on purpose: the e2e points the dev server at the Mux
# fake through vite.config.ts, and an empty value here would override it.
# MUX_API_URL (default https://api.mux.com) is a var, not a secret.
# MUX_TOKEN_ID=
# MUX_TOKEN_SECRET=
# MUX_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
#
# Phase 6 adds, for example:
# MOLLIE_API_KEY=
